# The classic six-node weighted graph from the README's worked example.
# Undirected roads with non-negative lengths. Load and run with:
#     python3 implementation.py cities.graph

edge A B 7
edge A C 9
edge A F 14
edge B C 10
edge B D 15
edge C D 11
edge C F 2
edge D E 6
edge E F 9

show

# Shortest route from A to E is A -> C -> F -> E, distance 20,
# even though the direct-looking A -> F edge costs 14 on its own.
path A E

# Every shortest distance out of A.
dist A
